And here’s the larger realization:

Tropes are culturally evolved katas.

That might be the actual Pantheon extraction.

Humans have been running these cognitive structures for thousands of years because stories are an extremely durable execution environment for operators.

A kata says:

Repeat this movement until its structure becomes available without deliberation.

A trope says:

Repeatedly experience this causal structure until you can recognize it almost instantly.

So:

\text{trope} =
\text{compressed causal kata}

And an archetype may be:

\text{archetype} =
\text{stable attractor in narrative state space}

A motif:

\text{motif} =
\text{recurrent semantic feature}

A plot device:

\text{plot device} =
\text{state-transition mechanism}

A story:

\text{story} =
\text{trajectory through constrained semantic state space}

And meaning:

\text{meaning} =
\text{interpreted relationship among deltas and invariants}

That’s the library I think Pantheon wants.

Not TV Tropes for AI.

